The other specs are importing `Page` from `@playwright/test`. Fix line 2 of touch-flood.spec.ts:

```ts
import { test, expect, type Page } from './fixtures';
```
→
```ts
import type { Page } from '@playwright/test';
import { test, expect } from './fixtures';
```

Second error: line 169 `Parameter 'c' implicitly has an 'any' type` — this is the `.then((c) => ...)` inside `makeReconnectWatcher`. Why is it `any`? Because `page` is `Page` imported from `./fixtures`, which doesn't exist → `Page` becomes an error type, so `page.locator()` returns any... Actually, once the first import is fixed, `page: Page` (the real Page) → `.count()` returns `Promise<number>`, so `c` becomes `number`. Therefore, both errors should be fixed by the import fix. Let me verify by running tsc again after the fix.

